# Application options. Zephyr requires the sourcing line at the end.

config BOSWELL_OPUS
	bool "Encode captured audio with Opus"
	default n
	help
	  Replaces IMA ADPCM with Opus in CELT restricted-low-delay mode.
	  Half the bitrate for considerably better audio: ADPCM is a 4-bit
	  quantiser at 64 kbps, Opus is near-transparent for speech at 32.

	  Costs about 190 KB of flash for the codec, so it is a build-time
	  choice rather than something the device switches at runtime. The
	  wire protocol carries a codec id either way, so a host can decode
	  recordings from a device built with or without this.

source "Kconfig.zephyr"
